        <mxCell id="cap" value="Figure 1. How JupyterHub runs. (1) The jupyterhub command starts the Hub, which reads jupyterhub_config.py and opens jupyterhub.sqlite. (2) The Hub launches configurable-http-proxy as a child process and writes the default route into it. (3) A browser request reaches the proxy, the only process on a public interface, and (4) the default route carries it to the Hub, where the Authenticator returns a username. (5) The Spawner, which runs inside the Hub process, launches jupyterhub-singleuser with an API token and polls it until it answers. (6) The Hub posts the new user route to the proxy admin API. (7, 8) After that the browser reaches the server through the proxy alone, so the Hub can be restarted without cutting a running session. (9) The server asks the Hub to check the browser token, cached for 300 s. The single-user port is random because Spawner.port defaults to 0. Repository commit not determined: this folder is not a git repository of its own." style="text;html=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=13;fontColor=#3c4043;fontFamily=Times New Roman;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="34" y="886" width="950" height="132" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
